 "reading": "Raising the prediction cap from 80 to 112 adds 140 A edges (1129 to 1269) and drops 0, so A is nested and the turnover is pure addition. K membership is not one number here. On the 12 16-tag seeds K is complete at both caps, so new and retained edges both sit at 1.000 and those seeds cannot answer the question. On larger-28 the new edges carry K at 0.812 (65 of 80) against 0.791 (394 of 498) for retained, a difference of +0.021, with 2 seeds above, 3 below and 1 tied (two-sided sign test p = 1.0000). The pooled rates move the other way (0.893 against 0.908, -0.015) only because the new edges are weighted toward larger-28 \u2014 80 of 140 against 498 of 1129 retained \u2014 whose base rate is lower; no block reverses that direction at block level. Against a block-adjusted expectation of 123.3, the new edges add 125 K-covered edges (+1.7), and joint C1 rises 1025 \u2192 1150.",
